c Pigeonhole principle: 4 pigeons, 3 holes
c Known UNSAT - classic hard instance for resolution
c Variables: x_{i,j} = pigeon i goes to hole j (1-indexed)
c x_{1,1}=1 x_{1,2}=2 x_{1,3}=3
c x_{2,1}=4 x_{2,2}=5 x_{2,3}=6
c x_{3,1}=7 x_{3,2}=8 x_{3,3}=9
c x_{4,1}=10 x_{4,2}=11 x_{4,3}=12
p cnf 12 22
c Each pigeon must go to at least one hole
1 2 3 0
4 5 6 0
7 8 9 0
10 11 12 0
c No two pigeons in the same hole
c Hole 1: at most one of {1,4,7,10}
-1 -4 0
-1 -7 0
-1 -10 0
-4 -7 0
-4 -10 0
-7 -10 0
c Hole 2: at most one of {2,5,8,11}
-2 -5 0
-2 -8 0
-2 -11 0
-5 -8 0
-5 -11 0
-8 -11 0
c Hole 3: at most one of {3,6,9,12}
-3 -6 0
-3 -9 0
-3 -12 0
-6 -9 0
-6 -12 0
-9 -12 0
